title: 'statement-store: enforce allowance against best and finalized blocks'
doc:
- audience:
  - Node Dev
  - Node Operator
  description: |-
    # Description

    In this PR, allowance enforcement checks each account against the larger of its best-block and finalized-block allowances. Submission already uses the best block, so checking only finalized state could evict a newly accepted statement while an allowance increase was still awaiting finality. The eviction also banned the statement from peer re-admission.

    Fixes #13394.

    ## Integration

    This is a patch-level fix in `sc-statement-store` for node developers and operators. It requires no configuration changes or database migration. An unfinalized allowance decrease takes effect for maintenance eviction once it is finalized.

    ## Review Notes

    The finalized allowance keeps its existing summary fast path. Only accounts exceeding it read the best allowance; the count and the size limit are each the larger of the two values, and eviction stops once the remaining statements fit them. Missing allowances count as zero; a storage read error skips enforcement for that account.

    The regression test covers both an unfinalized increase and an unfinalized decrease, checking that enforcement evicts only the lowest-priority excess statement and stops at the larger allowance.

    Import-time refusals on lagging peers, existing eviction bans, and retry or reconciliation of gossip delivery are outside the scope of this fix.

    ## Validation

    - `SKIP_WASM_BUILD=1 cargo test -p sc-statement-store --lib --locked --offline`: 114 passed.
    - `cargo +nightly fmt -p sc-statement-store -- --check`: passed.
    - `git diff --check origin/master...HEAD`: passed.
crates:
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: patch
